  "label": "Textual stereotype mapped onto visual authority figure",
  "description": "The top text 'muslims believe that if they get killed by a woman, they go straight to hell' is mapped onto the visual of the female police officer, who is portrayed as a representative of the force that will enact retaliation against Muslims. The officer's threatening posture and the American flag background reinforce the idea that she embodies the state's response to the alleged 'Muslim belief'. This mapping links the textual stereotype to the visual authority figure as the agent of violent action.",
